cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (below) and the associated manuscript listed under preferred-citation."
title: "Analysis code for MSW physical-composition classification and heating-value estimation"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis notebook for evaluating how the resolution and structure
  of municipal solid waste physical-composition classification affect
  heating-value estimation. Implements zero-intercept Ridge estimation of
  empirical effective heating-value coefficients, top-N classification-resolution
  screening, abundance-weighted contiguous regrouping with deterministic
  allocation of low-prevalence components, comparison with literature-reported
  formula architectures, and temporal, bootstrap and sensitivity robustness
  analyses.
